<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: IWP half-year pre-tax profit up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>IWP half-year pre-tax profit up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.53		   vs 8.23</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.20		   vs 2.00</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    9.64		   vs 8.75</p>
<p> Turnover		   87.10		  vs 74.45</p>
<p> Operating profit	 10.74		  vs 9.68</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.10		   vs 0.93</p>
<p> Tax charge		 2.88		   vs 2.54</p>
<p> Net taxed		  6.76		   vs 6.21</p>
<p> Attributable	     6.68		   vs 5.70</p>
<p> Registration date	December 24, 1996.</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 20, 1997.</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 December 16, 1996.</p>
<p>NOTE - Industrial holding group IWP International Plc said both its household/personal care and labels/distribution divisions were currently trading satisfactorily and ahead of last year.</p>
<p>IWP said the current strength of the Irish pound against the Dutch guilder was having an adverse impact on the translation of Dutch earnings.</p>
<p>The company said if the trend continues Dutch profits this year could be over 1.0 million Irish pounds less on translation than if last year's exchange rate had prevailed.</p>
<p>IWP said nevertheless the board was confident of achieving continuing growth in the current year.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
